        "section": [
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">COPD exacerbation, treated with bronchodilators and steroids</div>"
            },
            "code": {
              "coding": [
                {
                  "code": "67781-5",
                  "system": "http://loinc.org",
                  "display": "Summarization of encounter note"
                }
              ]
            },
            "title": "Synthesis"
          },
          {
            "text": {
              "status": "generated",
              "div": "<div xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 85-year-old male patient, admitted on 06/10/2025 due to an acute exacerbation of his known chronic obstructive pulmonary disease. On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Clinical examination, chest X-ray, arterial blood gas analysis, and pulse oximetry confirmed an acute exacerbation. Blood tests revealed mild systemic inflammation. The patient was treated with inhaled bronchodilators via nebulizer, systemic corticosteroids, and supplemental oxygen therapy, leading to significant clinical improvement. Vital signs were monitored closely throughout the stay. Prior to discharge, patient education regarding inhaler technique and exacerbation management was provided. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close follow-up in your practice. Please do not hesitate to contact me should you require further information.</div>"
            },
